[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. Read the
bodies and the reports describe three different problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes only one of them. The booking-v3 hint and the one-day move stay broken
until they get their own fix.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/Julka768/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/Julka768/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    'one-day move': 'https://github.com/Julka768/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

- **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the
  day first. 7 April comes out as 4 July.
- **hint**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month
  first, as told, and the form reads the day first. Same swap, different bug: a parser fix does
  not reach it.
- **one-day move**: the date moves by one day, or differs by time zone ("Client in Lisbon got
  Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). No day and month swap at all. The desk already listed
  these in `desk-notes.json`, then filed them under the parser.

## How a report is placed

1. One id, one report. The export repeats some reports.
2. On the desk's one-day-move list: **one-day move**.
3. Came through the form at a tenant that runs booking-v3: **hint**.
4. Any other report from a day-first tenant: **parser**.

The tenant decides, not intake. `meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser and is
not used here.

## Why one ticket hid three

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on the subject line alone.
All three problems arrive under the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"),
so the rule could never tell them apart. Only the body and the tenant can. A decision is not
edited after it is accepted, so a change to that rule needs a new record.

